; THE POINT OF SP-ERM-e-SSI, in one function.
;
; A bounds-checked array access whose check is REDUNDANT, and where the
; redundancy is visible as a property of NAMES rather than of program
; points. .ll cannot state any of the three facts below in its text form.
;
;   E  the pi node names "the index, on the path where the check passed"
;   R  every version carries its range, so `i < 16` after `i in [0,7]`
;      is decidably true without re-running an analysis
;   M  the load names the store version it reads, so a later pass knows
;      exactly what it observes without rebuilding MemorySSA
;
; The array has 16 elements. `i` is masked to 4 bits, so it is provably
; in [0,15] before the check ever runs.
module bounds
func get pub entry=entry
  block entry
    %1 = param name=arr             [null=nonnull]
    %2 = param name=i
    %3 = const.int ival=15
    %4 = bin %2 %3 op=and           ; i & 15  ->  provably [0,15]
    %5 = const.int ival=16
    %6 = bin %4 %5 op=lt            ; ALWAYS true; R can prove it
    branch %6 ok fail
  end
  block ok
    ; pi: the index on the non-faulting path. Carries inbounds.
    %7 = pi %4 %6 fact=inbounds
    %8 = load.index %1 %7
    ret %8
  end
  block fail
    trap
  end
endfunc
